														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2802897">
									

<p>This was great. I got quiet tingles. Soft, insidious effect, never trying to break into anything overstated or plot-twisty. &quot;I don't know. The door was unlocked&quot; fucked me up in all the right ways.</p>
<p>One thing I don't like - placing it inside a cave, and having the opening be a picture of a cave entrance. O, Death and Somewhere In the Between both did it, and I think a version of The Reliquary had it too for a while. The first two times I opened this page, I saw a cave entrance and checked out. I feel like this would be much better served with a picture of the room, or no picture at all (though I know Roget would hate the latter). Doesn't change my upvote, tho.</p>

							</div>

								
					
